--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

ADE contains no third-party code.

Its OFS/FFS/RDB handling is an independent implementation written from
public format documentation — Laurent Clévy's ".ADF format FAQ", the Linux
kernel AFFS driver documentation, and RKRM: Devices Appendix C. ADFlib is
used only as a black-box differential-test oracle: invoked as a separate
binary by the test harness, never linked, and its source deliberately not
read (see DECISIONS.md, D-002). No ADFlib code or GPL obligation is
inherited.

Should a future decision introduce third-party code — D-009 contemplates a
possible port of xDMS — the attribution belongs here.
